Subject: Allow FluxInstance preflight on DHI Debian and Alpine

Flux Operator rejects FluxInstance reconciliation unless its container OS is explicitly allowed. Recognize the Debian 13 and Alpine 3 bases used by the DHI package while preserving the existing distroless and RHEL checks.

Origin: DHI-internal (DHI runtime compatibility)
Description: Add the DHI Debian and Alpine base identities to Flux Operator's container OS preflight allowlist.
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/controlplaneio-fluxcd/flux-operator.git 8e761853ba15347181cee6cb23e7c9e622e2a93d
Verify: test internal/entitlement/preflight_test.go::TestCheckOSMinimumVersion
Forwarded: no (upstream closed issue 1074 as not planned)
Drop-When: never: upstream declined support for third-party hardened images and this compatibility remains DHI-owned

diff --git a/internal/controller/fluxinstance_controller.go b/internal/controller/fluxinstance_controller.go
index 442390f..89a4aa0 100644
--- a/internal/controller/fluxinstance_controller.go
+++ b/internal/controller/fluxinstance_controller.go
@@ -161,6 +161,8 @@ func (r *FluxInstanceReconciler) reconcile(ctx context.Context,
 		entitlement.WithMinVersion("2.2.0"),
 		entitlement.WithContainerOS("distroless", 12),
 		entitlement.WithContainerOS("rhel", 8),
+		entitlement.WithContainerOS("debian", 13),
+		entitlement.WithContainerOS("alpine", 3),
 	); err != nil {
 		// If this happens, then the operator image has been tampered with
 		// e.g.: the manifests are missing, or the Flux / OS version is not supported.
